      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dickinson College, chartered in 1773 by Benjamin Rush, is the first college founded after the United States was founded.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlisle%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1879, Lieutenant Richard Henry Pratt opened Carlisle Indian Industrial School, the first federally supported school for American Indians off a reservation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlisle%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A cannonball dent still marks one of the columns of Carlisle’s historic county courthouse, a relic from colonial skirmishes.",
